WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
(June, the 43rd of Shinka Era
 Yokosuka)

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:04.040
Aw, shucks.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.370
Is that the Antares or whatever?

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:07.700
Naw, not that one.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.860
Antares is some
 state-of-the-art submarine.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.910
All this riot, just because
 it's coming to Yokosuka.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:20.040
It can't stay at Ogasawara since
 Ogasawara will be returned to Japan.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.880
Hey, you. No diving here.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.540
Is he a superhuman?

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:15.250
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.500
I heard it
 A voice cursing fate

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:26.660
I found it
 A way to use my power

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:30.410
What you want are not words,
 are they?

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.870
That love inside
 I want to send it on

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.650
Justice is not on my side

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:41.000
The only thing absolute for me
 is myself

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.620
Come on Wakers. Ready, go!

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.500
Protecting the illusions
 that somebody dreamed of

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:53.120
will liberate the stagnant sky

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:58.750
We hurl our unanswerable cries
 at each other

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.580
And they become the reason we live

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:09.250
What can I do in this
 hopeless world we live in?

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:14.330
Only those that keep searching

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.160
can become the future

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:21.160
Start the revolution!

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.160
"Justice/Freedom/Peace"

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.500
Hello, Hitoyoshi residence.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:35.540
Oh, Chinatsu-san?

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.500
Hi Kikko-chan. How've you been?

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.330
Is Jiro-san, I mean, is Senpai home?

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:45.120
Jiro-san's been gone
 since early this morning.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.120
Senpai...

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.750
Kikko-chan, where are you?

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:52.580
Oh, just tell him to
 call the office if you see him.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.080
Oh yeah, about Jiro-san.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.080
Did I tell you that he can
 only eat non-spicy curry?

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.580
Isn't it about time we wake them up?

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.870
This is going too far
 even for students.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:09.200
But our job today is to just
 watch over the Angel Stars.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:16.370
Where did Senpai and Miss Emi go?

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.700
Maybe a date.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.540
Kikko, if you put your mind to it,

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:25.200
Mr. Jiro would ditch Ogre Emi.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:26.580
Kikko?

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.540
Hello? Kikko?

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.390
Is she that bad?

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.040
Excuse me?

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.400
Emi. Do you hate her that much?

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.030
May I be honest, sir?

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:40.410
Sure.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.200
She's a pretty person.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.540
Not really a person...

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.660
Oh, right.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.660
And as your assistant...

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.370
She's incredible.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:54.040
You could say the study of superhuman
 folklorist formed thanks to her.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.420
- That's why...
 - Why what?

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:00.540
Maybe Mr. Jiro can't
 say no to her sometimes.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:06.910
Thank you.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.270
For worrying about Jiro.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.150
You don't understand, do you?

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.080
Our offer is on par
 with the Angel Stars.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.660
But if you have any requests...

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.160
Add as many zeros as you like.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:39.840
Last winter...

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.620
Teito Advertisement Inc. tried to
 distribute an Anitsuperhuman-Element.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:45.910
A man died.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.040
And before that was the beast.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:51.540
You tried to start a beast craze.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:55.200
To make people become
 in favor of beasts.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.000
And you regard the Bureau
 as an enemy.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.230
Superhumans too.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.660
That's a misunderstanding.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.990
We believe in the theory that
 superhumans evolved from humans.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:08.750
Humans?

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:13.790
Don't you think the Bureau has
 interpreted superhumans too broadly?

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:17.290
Superhumans are just
 another form of humans.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.450
Not aliens, goblins,
 monsters, nor robots.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.420
Much less yokai.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:28.760
Superhumans protect justice.
 The hope of human evolution.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.000
More importantly, do your research.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.000
I'm not a superhuman.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.950
I don't have any superpowers.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:44.950
Jiro!

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.150
You guys, Yokosuka is in trouble.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.330
Full of freaks.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.540
But they won't make it in time now.
 It's enough.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.750
But Advisor Satomi, can we trust him?

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.870
You mean Claude?

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:10.500
He questions the existence of
 the Bureau itself.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.580
An existing question.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.750
You guys again.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.410
We haven't done anything.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:23.980
This could get dangerous.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.250
Cooperate!

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.700
What the heck?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:34.290
Don't laugh!

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.160
It's the superhuman detective.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.450
I am leaving alone.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.580
He's singing?

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.380
- You're right.
 - He's broken.

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:53.010
Many among you infringe
 the Secret Functional Law.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.700
Like the tragedy at Haneda...

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:58.140
It's the cops that killed him!

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.700
No, it was the violent students
 against the EDC.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.000
Superhuman detective.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.790
Are you for Japan's participation
 in the EDC?

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.530
All aliens will be considered enemies.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.950
Superhuman folk music?

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:21.080
Time for the U.S. Navy's latest
 Antares to make its appearance.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:32.950
What the...?

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.790
Wait, wait, wait, once again

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:01.120
I get to have the first word

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:05.450
With that indecisive kiss

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:09.620
Blast away everything and anything

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:12.120
Tick-tock, tick-tock, boom

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.090
Your warmth...

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.700
So who are you?

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:19.850
Don't do such a terrible thing.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:22.700
Tell me, beautiful superhumans.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.350
Beautiful, huh?

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:27.700
Do you fight for justice?

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:28.870
Or for peace?

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:31.240
Or for the freedom of humanity?

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.200
I'd say justice.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:35.370
But nothing's better than peace.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.620
And paychecks.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.740
Good answer.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.750
Why do you ask?

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.700
My name is Claude.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.250
Misterious-Sword Claude.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:05.620
Claude?

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.310
Of what organization?

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:10.320
Detective Raito Shiba.
 I am a superhuman.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.120
That's what they all say.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:13.440
I'll arrest you.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:27.910
Are you okay, Angels?

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.910
What's your purpose?

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.220
Do you know the real identity
 of that submarine?

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:42.220
It got a dramatic boost in performance
 by boarding superhumans.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.330
A dramatic capability to kill.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:46.660
To fight wars.

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:50.000
What's wrong, Hoshinoko?

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.000
Superhumans aren't for
 conflicts between countries.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.330
Neither for using them
 to battle each other.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:13.660
Should you not use what you believe
 and strive for a better future?

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:17.010
Is it nonsense?

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.290
Yeah, if you're just babbling alone.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.250
One single person
 can change the world.

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:26.450
Is that just a fantasy
 all superhumans dream of?

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:27.750
But I...

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:45.910
My body is a factory that can
 metamorphose metals.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:50.170
Just like the factories moving now
 all over this country.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:56.620
You're going to fight all alone?

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:58.970
Those wanting to use
 superhumans for war?

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:01.720
Freedom...

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:04.700
Peace...

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:07.600
Or justice.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:13.580
The only worthy reasons
 for superhumans to fight.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:17.070
And not for one's self,
 but for the people.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.000
Right on.

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:23.070
And your choice, Mr. Shiba?

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.540
I will not condone superhuman crimes.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:26.660
Nothing more.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.910
Could he be...?

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:37.160
What?

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.700
Nothing.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:41.680
We should help Mr. Shiba, right?

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:45.050
Setting channel to witch power.
 Meteortail!

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:50.500
- It's a witch!
 - Get a camera.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:53.690
Well, Reiichi?
 She's of the Bureau, right?

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:00.120
Miss Kikko Hoshino!

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:03.950
Who is that? I'm just a passerby.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.290
I don't mean to fight you.
 You're a righteous superhuman.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:20.660
Hoshinoko.

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:21.910
Hoshinoko!

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:28.790
That power...

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:35.700
Kikko.

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:36.870
Hey, Kikko.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.190
Wake up.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:46.370
Jiro Senpai...

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.530
You've come to.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.410
Senpai.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.200
What's wrong, Miss Kikko?

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.910
I'm embarrassed.
 I want to stay buried.

00:12:57.950 --> 00:12:59.700
You can't.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.540
There's trouble. See?

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:10.510
Don't take pictures! Gimme that.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:14.390
I was just changing it.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.580
Everybody, look.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:20.750
Oh my gosh.

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:25.290
This afternoon, a submarine was
 attacked by an assailant.

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:28.080
It was the U.S. Navy's
 cutting edge submarine.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.580
This is the inside of U.S.S. Antares.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:35.160
The U.S.S. Antares is the world's
 first Superhumanic-Submarine.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:39.830
It was part of the Master Commander
 Plan associated with Master Ultima.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:44.660
According to footage taken by chance,
 humans were stuck between machines...

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:47.700
This news breaks
 the Secret Functional Law.

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:49.950
I suppose some strings were pulled.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.370
Teito Publicity, I bet.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.930
Who's that Skull-man in the cape?

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.020
It's not a skull. It's Claude.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.040
Misterious-Sword Claude.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:04.370
It was to expose how the U.S. Army's
 use of superhumans was inhumane, huh?

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:07.120
That should've been our job.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.870
A summons?

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:18.200
So you'll be fine
 if you go to that doctor?

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.040
Thank you for taking me.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:22.540
I see.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:25.040
So about that Claude guy's powers.

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:28.760
He said his body was a metal factory.

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:30.290
And...

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:36.450
What is it?

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.290
I don't know how to say it.

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:43.570
Think Equus can beat him?

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.870
You're going to fight him?

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:47.040
Of course.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.160
Over 70 people died
 just in the U.S. Army.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:55.700
But the submarine crew
 was already dead.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.830
They might've been machine parts.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:00.200
You're right.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.950
Chief will probably have
 a talk about it with them later.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.830
Those crew members.

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:09.370
Weren't they superhumans that
 we should've protected?

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:11.720
I would've if I'd known.

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.000
Really?

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:16.330
But is that reason to forgive Claude?

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.450
He might be in league with Teito.

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:21.480
Why else would TV be there?

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:24.660
But Teito is just a publicity firm.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:26.730
Why are you so hostile?

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:28.870
That's because...

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:31.540
Superhumans are just
 another form of humans.

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:35.490
Anyway, Claude isn't a superhuman.
 He's a demon.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:36.910
I'm a witch!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.910
I know! That's why...

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:43.830
Stop the car.

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:45.460
But the doctor...

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.210
I said stop.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.120
Sorry I'm late.

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:02.600
(June, 43rd of Shinka Era
 Yoron Newspaper)

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.610
It's not just us?

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:07.750
It's an emergency.

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:10.740
It's the Bureau's fault
 for letting that monster free.

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:12.000
But that's...

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:17.830
He was the Commissioner of the
 Ministry of Defense until recently.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.160
I'm Mitsuya.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.540
Mr. Akita of the Super Population
 Research Laboratory?

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.830
He's helping us with
 the Revised Secret Functional Law.

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:30.000
The one submitted by
 the Health and Welfare Ministry.

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:32.580
AKA a superhuman law.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:34.160
Yes, I'm for it.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:40.870
A word, but the Japanese government

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:45.310
uses superhumans secretively
 in the Public Security Force.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:49.120
These things would be banned
 with a new superhuman law.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:51.120
No, it won't be.

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:55.320
They'll be able to join by
 registering as a superhuman.

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:57.070
That's why I'm for it.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:00.120
Defense, foreign affairs,
 law enforcement...

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.950
Sir Mitsuya is wrapping up
 the talks with all quarters.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.080
But to do that.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.750
We can't have long-haired
 singing superhuman students

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:12.840
being influenced like this.

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:16.340
Are you suggesting a quid pro quo?

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.660
We will discuss things
 extensively with the U.S.

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:26.250
But we will deal strongly with that
 mutant Claude.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:30.080
He exposed that the Antares
 was an inhumane weapon.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:32.790
Some say he's a superhuman of justice.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:34.910
If he's justice,

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:38.740
then the U.S. Army,
 and Japan who supports it, are evil.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:44.000
He really got you good, huh?

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:54.380
Hey, no funny stuff.

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:56.160
Don't worry.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:59.390
Highly developed magic
 is equal to science.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.010
Our magic is science.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:05.450
We're contracted by
 the police department.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.620
Relax and leave it to us.

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:12.270
Then help me.
 I want to expose what Claude is.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:13.790
Leave it to us.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:16.200
There are no mysteries
 that can't be solved.

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:19.250
That's the credo for us Sciencers.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:22.450
The Bureau will protect even him, huh.

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:29.040
(August, the 43rd of Shinka Era
 Hokkaido)

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.700
Are you really going alone, Hoshinoko?

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:37.000
Miss Kikko Hoshino.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.660
There's something I want you to see.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:51.330
What if he only wants
 me to know about it?

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:53.870
If it turns out to be nothing,

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.940
tonight's miso-flavor noodle
 will be on you.

00:18:57.290 --> 00:19:00.950
These 2 months,
 we've heard nothing from Claude.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:28.830
Meteortail.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.200
What are you doing here?

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.050
How can you...?

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:07.410
Why?

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:18.950
- Hoshinoko!
 - I'm hot.

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:20.950
I'm hot, I'm so hot.

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:22.790
I'm so hot!

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:23.870
Stop!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.700
Ullr, I think I've
 caught a cold again.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.370
I'm so hot.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:29.790
Is that...?

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:04.160
Hoshinoko.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:08.660
Ullr. I command you.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:10.830
Bring me my Tail of a Meteor.

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:26.080
Answer me, human.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.390
What is this lawlessness?

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:31.750
Hear me, future Queen
 of the Demon's World.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:34.640
Somebody had to do this.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:38.080
Justice?

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:41.400
As a superhuman,
 I cannot condone evil.

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:44.900
I must fight true evil.

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:53.450
Tell me, Claude.

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:56.870
Are you...

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:59.370
somebody I know?

00:22:03.580 --> 00:22:04.620
Yes.

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:15.370
I knew it.

00:23:56.500 --> 00:23:59.330
Wishing for freedom may disrupt peace.

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:01.950
Justice fights justice for peace.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:05.080
Again today,
 your justice violates my freedom.

00:24:05.120 --> 00:24:08.000
Answer me. Why do you fight?

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:10.870
My name is Claude.
 Misterious-Sword Claude.
